# Git workflow (agents)

## Branches

1. Run `git branch --show-current` before creating or switching branches.
2. Base feature work off `main`.
3. Commit messages and PR titles/bodies: **English only**.

## Commit, push, PR — only when the user says so

- **Never** `git commit`, `git push`, or `gh pr create` unless the user
  **explicitly** asked in **this** turn (`commit`, `push`, `open a PR`).
- A plan todo such as “commit, PR”, “finish all todos”, or “implement the plan”
  is **not** permission to commit or push.
- **Never** offer commit or push (“say the word if you want a commit”). Leave
  the tree dirty. The user will ask if they want it.

## Protected main

- **Never** `git push origin main` (or force-push to `main`).
- All changes land via **pull request** into `main`.

## Auto-resync after merge (mandatory — do not wait to be asked)

The user merging a PR on GitHub is enough. Do **not** wait for "switch back to main" / "pull".

Run this at **session start** and **before starting any new task**. If **you** merge the PR in this turn, run it in the same turn.

Always `git fetch origin` first.

If already on `main` and `origin/main` is ahead: `git merge --ff-only origin/main`. Do not wait to be asked to pull.

If the current branch is not `main`:

1. Treat the current branch as merged if either:
   - `gh pr view --json state --jq .state` is `MERGED`, or
   - `git merge-base --is-ancestor HEAD origin/main` succeeds (this branch is fully contained in `origin/main`)
2. If **not** merged: stay on the feature branch.
3. If merged, point local `main` at `origin/main` (local `main` is often behind; a plain `git checkout main` can overwrite uncommitted files):

```bash
git checkout -B main origin/main
git branch -d <feature-branch>
# Remote may already be gone (GitHub "Automatically delete head branches").
git push origin --delete <feature-branch>  # ignore errors if already deleted
```

Uncommitted files come along when they apply cleanly. If that checkout **fails** (would overwrite dirty files): stop. Do not stash, discard, or reset. Report the dirty paths.

If `git branch -d` refuses, use `git branch -D` only after confirming the PR is merged into `main`.

## PR lifecycle (only after an explicit user request)

1. Implement on a feature branch off `main`
2. Commit, push, create/update PR — **only if the user asked**
3. Merge when asked
4. Auto-resync after a merged PR as above — no extra user prompt
   (resync must not commit or push the agent’s own uncommitted work)
